    "answer": {
      "short": "Mary has only $4$ candidates, $\\pm1,\\pm101$, whereas Bob has $16$.\n\nPossible integer zeroes are factors of the constant term; $101$ is prime.",
      "worked": "By the integer root theorem, any integer zero must divide the constant term $c$.\n\nFor Mary, $101$ is prime, so the only candidates are $\\pm1$ and $\\pm101$: four values.\n\nFor Bob, the candidates are $\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,\\pm4,\\pm6,\\pm8,\\pm12,\\pm24$: sixteen values.\n\nMary is happy because she has fewer candidates to test.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
